{{!-- `always-interactive` is required, not decorative: a looter does not own the chest, so
      the sheet renders read-only and every control without this class is disabled. What the
      button does is re-validated GM-side by the transfer kernel's takeFromContainer, so the
      class grants an affordance, never a permission.
      Item rows only — see shelf-hide.hbs for why activity rows need the guard. --}}
<div class="item-detail item-lootTake" data-column-id="lootTake">
    {{#if isItem}}
    <button type="button" class="lootshelf-action-button always-interactive" data-action="take"
            aria-label="Take {{ item.name }}">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-hand-holding" inert></i>
        <span>Take</span>
    </button>
    {{/if}}
</div>
